WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.039
Orange flames danced near the wolves.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.846
They backed away in terror.

3
00:00:06.847 --> 00:00:10.606
"I'm leaving the jungle!" Mowgli yelled.

4
00:00:10.607 --> 00:00:13.412
"I'm going to live in the village.

5
00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.429
The humans will be kind to me."

6
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.879
He stepped toward a pile of sticks.

7
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:24.019
"Now I must pay a debt."

8
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:30.035
He grabbed a stick and lit it from the fire.

9
00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:36.558
Then he marched toward Shere Khan and held the stick close to the tiger's fur.

10
00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:41.204
"Remember this, Shere Khan." Mowgli growled.

11
00:00:41.205 --> 00:00:48.065
"The next time I come to Council Rock, I will be carrying your hide."

12
00:00:48.066 --> 00:00:52.118
He waved the burning stick even closer to the tiger.

13
00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:57.313
"And Akela goes free. You will not kill him!"

14
00:00:57.314 --> 00:01:01.392
The fire burned furiously at the end of the stick.

15
00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:07.649
Mowgli waved it right and left, and the frightened tiger ran off.

16
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:13.736
Most of the wolves ran off too, howling as sparks landed on their fur.

17
00:01:13.737 --> 00:01:17.593
Akela and Bagheera hurried over to Mowgli.

18
00:01:17.594 --> 00:01:26.050
He was gasping in pain, and tears streamed down his face.

19
00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:30.106
"What's happening to me, Bagheera?" he said.

20
00:01:30.107 --> 00:01:34.054
"Why do I feel so strange?"

21
00:01:34.055 --> 00:01:37.274
"You are feeling deep sorrow, Little Brother.

22
00:01:37.275 --> 00:01:39.529
That is why you are crying.

23
00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:43.083
Only humans shed tears like yours."

24
00:01:43.084 --> 00:01:50.936
Mowgli sat and cried for a while.

25
00:01:50.937 --> 00:01:53.467
Finally he got up.

26
00:01:53.468 --> 00:01:56.340
"I'm going back to the cave now.

27
00:01:56.341 --> 00:02:03.047
In the morning I will say farewell to Mother and Father Wolf."

28
00:02:03.048 --> 00:02:10.561
The next day the young wolves howled miserably as Mowgli stood at the mouth of the cave.

29
00:02:10.562 --> 00:02:14.414
"You won't forget me, will you?" Mowgli said.

30
00:02:14.415 --> 00:02:18.638
"Never!" the one named Gray Brother promised.

31
00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:22.113
"Meet us at the bottom of the hill every once in a while.

32
00:02:22.114 --> 00:02:24.573
We can play with you there."

33
00:02:24.574 --> 00:02:29.115
"We will miss you, Mowgli," Mother said softly.

34
00:02:29.116 --> 00:02:33.201
"I will meet you soon," Mowgli promised.

35
00:02:33.202 --> 00:02:39.704
Then he left the cave and went down the hillside alone.

36
00:02:39.705 --> 00:02:45.950
Mowgli walked for hours along a rough road that ran down the valley.

37
00:02:45.951 --> 00:02:51.198
At last, the road opened into a wide plain.

38
00:02:51.199 --> 00:02:55.797
The plain was dotted with big rocks and trees.

39
00:02:55.798 --> 00:03:00.711
Herds of cattle and buffalo grazed all over the plain.

40
00:03:00.712 --> 00:03:06.801
In the distance Mowgli could see a village.

41
00:03:06.802 --> 00:03:14.111
Several children were in charge of the animal herds.

42
00:03:14.112 --> 00:03:21.219
When they saw Mowgli, they shouted in fear and ran away.

43
00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:26.738
Hungry, Mowgli headed toward the village.

44
00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:31.235
When he reached the gate, a man came out.

45
00:03:31.236 --> 00:03:36.829
Mowgli opened his mouth and pointed down it to show that he was hungry.

46
00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:41.323
The man stared in shock and spun around.

47
00:03:41.324 --> 00:03:44.987
He ran away, shouting for the priest.

48
00:03:44.988 --> 00:03:50.985
Soon a big, fat man dressed in white came to the gate.

49
00:03:50.986 --> 00:03:54.279
He had a colorful mark on his forehead.

50
00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.932
Behind him was a huge crowd.

51
00:03:56.933 --> 00:04:00.377
They all stared and pointed at Mowgli.

52
00:04:00.378 --> 00:04:04.495
"Humans have no manners," Mowgli thought.

53
00:04:04.496 --> 00:04:11.221
"Only monkeys behave like this!" He frowned at the crowd.

54
00:04:11.222 --> 00:04:17.200
"There's nothing to be afraid of," the priest said to the crowd.

55
00:04:17.201 --> 00:04:19.535
He pointed to Mowgli.

56
00:04:19.536 --> 00:04:25.031
"Look at these marks on the boy's arms and legs.

57
00:04:25.032 --> 00:04:26.962
They are wolf bites.

58
00:04:26.963 --> 00:04:31.404
He has probably run away from the jungle."

59
00:04:31.405 --> 00:04:35.754
"The poor child!" a few women said.

60
00:04:35.755 --> 00:04:40.375
"He is a handsome boy," a woman said.

61
00:04:40.376 --> 00:04:44.147
Suddenly one woman gasped.

62
00:04:44.148 --> 00:04:46.911
"Messua! He looks like your boy!

63
00:04:46.912 --> 00:04:50.331
The one who was stolen by the tiger!"

64
00:04:50.332 --> 00:04:55.671
A woman with copper rings on her wrists and ankles stepped forward.

65
00:04:55.672 --> 00:04:58.572
She looked closely at Mowgli.

66
00:04:58.573 --> 00:05:03.503
"I'm not sure if he's my boy," she said at last.

67
00:05:03.504 --> 00:05:06.551
"But he does look like my son."

68
00:05:06.552 --> 00:05:09.632
The priest threw up his arms.

69
00:05:09.633 --> 00:05:15.294
"What the jungle has taken, the jungle has returned!

70
00:05:15.295 --> 00:05:21.067
Take the child home, Messua."

